WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.432
A multi-agent system is a program that divides work among several AI helpers.

00:00:06.432 --> 00:00:10.287
Each specialist can have its own instructions and tools.

00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:15.077
Think of a shop with a wholesale desk and a separate inventory desk.

00:00:15.077 --> 00:00:22.247
A coordinator reads the request, decides who should handle each part, and brings the results together.

00:00:22.247 --> 00:00:27.998
A handoff is the act of passing a task and the information needed to complete it.

00:00:27.998 --> 00:00:35.209
A framework supplies reusable software for running the helpers and passing messages between them.

00:00:35.209 --> 00:00:39.222
It does not decide whether your team needs more helpers.

00:00:39.222 --> 00:00:44.748
That choice depends on which problems a single helper is actually having.

00:00:44.748 --> 00:00:51.439
A customer asks Orbit about terms for buying tents in bulk and whether enough tents are available.

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:53.909
There are two facts to establish.

00:00:53.909 --> 00:00:57.006
The wholesale rules describe the terms.

00:00:57.006 --> 00:01:00.743
The inventory record shows the quantity available.

00:01:00.743 --> 00:01:07.313
Knowing one cannot establish the other, so the coordinator keeps the two questions separate.

00:01:07.313 --> 00:01:10.625
Splitting is not free, so weigh it honestly.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:16.901
One agent means one prompt and one loop to test, and the fewest model calls per answer.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:23.005
Its weakness is crowding: as tools and jobs pile up, it starts to mix them up.

00:01:23.005 --> 00:01:31.670
Several agents get small, focused prompts, but every request now pays for extra calls to route it and hand it over.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:40.056
There are also more places to break, and one customer's trace now spans several agents, so debugging takes longer.

00:01:40.056 --> 00:01:47.535
The rule of thumb: start with one agent, measure it, and split only when your tests show it struggling.

00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:54.311
It sends the buying question to the wholesale helper and the stock question to the inventory helper.

00:01:54.311 --> 00:01:57.814
Each needs the item and requested quantity.

00:01:57.814 --> 00:02:03.973
When the results return, the coordinator can combine the terms with the available quantity.

00:02:03.973 --> 00:02:12.475
If the inventory answer is missing, it should say availability is unconfirmed rather than promise the order.

00:02:12.475 --> 00:02:15.616
Here is one request moving through the team.

00:02:15.616 --> 00:02:20.262
A shop owner asks for forty green two person tents for their store.

00:02:20.262 --> 00:02:27.378
The coordinator classifies it as wholesale and passes a short summary to the wholesale agent.

00:02:27.378 --> 00:02:33.320
The wholesale agent checks stock and finds only four of those tents in the warehouse.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:40.032
It replies honestly with what is available and hands the rest of the order to Maya to confirm.

00:02:40.032 --> 00:02:48.105
Notice that agents pass short summaries to each other rather than whole conversations, which keeps every call small.

00:02:48.105 --> 00:02:51.075
Read the shop owner's enquiry twice.

00:02:51.075 --> 00:02:56.282
How many green tents can Orbit supply, and under what wholesale terms?

00:02:56.282 --> 00:03:02.695
Being able to answer the terms does not establish that forty tents are physically available.

00:03:02.695 --> 00:03:08.524
Give the inventory helper a narrow question with the exact style, colour and quantity.

00:03:08.524 --> 00:03:11.812
Four available now is useful evidence.

00:03:11.812 --> 00:03:18.876
It is not permission for the wholesale helper to promise the remaining thirty-six on a particular date.

00:03:18.876 --> 00:03:25.289
The coordinator can report the confirmed quantity and hand the outstanding question to Maya.

00:03:25.289 --> 00:03:28.622
Read the joined reply as the shop owner.

00:03:28.622 --> 00:03:34.863
It should be clear which part you can count on today and which part still needs confirmation.

00:03:34.863 --> 00:03:39.058
Run the same request through one assistant with both tools.

00:03:39.058 --> 00:03:46.962
Compare the accuracy of the answer, how long it took, and whether the item and quantity survived each handoff.

00:03:46.962 --> 00:03:52.330
The extra specialists earn their place only if they solve a measurable problem.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:57.686
Extra messages by themselves do not make the service more capable.
